# SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0
#
# The antr_* adapter's Kconfig, shared between every application that links
# radiant's "core" backend: rsourced by the root Kconfig, by strap/Kconfig
# and by radiant/tests/api/Kconfig, the same way src/node/Kconfig and
# src/profiles/Kconfig already are.
#
# WHY THIS FILE EXISTS, SEPARATELY FROM radiant/Kconfig: both symbols
# below used to live there, because src/radiant_api.c and src/radiant_sec_host.c
# used to be compiled AS PART OF the radiant module (Kconfig-gated with
# zephyr_library_sources_ifdef()). They have moved out - to
# src/ant_radio_radiant.c and src/ant_sec_host.c - because they are, and always
# were, the seam between radiant and the ANT serial protocol rather than
# core module material: the one file (each) that reaches an application
# header. Their Kconfig symbols moved with them, for the same reason
# CONFIG_ANT_DONGLE_RADIO_* lives in the root Kconfig and not in any module's:
# a symbol that gates an application source list belongs in that application's
# Kconfig tree, not in a Zephyr module meant to be dropped into a project with
# nothing else from this repository on its include path.
#
# The symbol NAMES did not change - only where they are declared - so nothing
# that already says CONFIG_RADIANT_ANTR_API or
# CONFIG_RADIANT_SEC_HOST_MESSAGES (a .conf fragment, a testcase.yaml
# extra_configs block, a comment) needed to change with them.

config RADIANT_ANTR_API
	bool "compile the antr_* adapter (src/ant_radio_radiant.c)"
	default y
	depends on RADIANT
	help
	  src/ant_radio_radiant.c is the integration layer: it implements the
	  fifty antr_* entry points that src/ant_radio.h declares, on top of
	  radiant's modules. It used to be compiled as part of the
	  radiant Zephyr module, gated by this very symbol under a
	  zephyr_library_sources_ifdef() there; it moved out so the module
	  never has to reach an application header to build - see
	  radiant/include/radiant/radiant_msg.h for what replaced
	  the reach-through this adapter used to provide from inside the
	  module.

	  radiant/tests/api sets this to y unconditionally in its own
	  CMakeLists.txt now (not through this symbol - see that file) because
	  compiling the adapter is the whole point of that application; the
	  parent radiant/tests suite never adds it at all, for the
	  opposite reason - its suites test the modules, not the forwarding,
	  and compiling the adapter there would drag src/ant_radio.h's whole
	  surface into a build that has no bridge to satisfy it.

config RADIANT_SEC_HOST_MESSAGES
	bool "compile the 0xF1-0xF5 host messages"
	default y
	depends on RADIANT_ANTR_API && RADIANT_SEC
	help
	  src/ant_sec_host.c: the antr_sec_* adapter behind message IDs 0xF1
	  (configure), 0xF2 (set key), 0xF3 (epoch), 0xF4 (status) and 0xF5
	  (pairing). Mirrors RADIANT_ANTR_API's gate - this is the one
	  security file that reaches an application header - and depends on
	  RADIANT_SEC directly now that it no longer lives inside that
	  symbol's `if` block in radiant/Kconfig; moving here took it out
	  from under that nesting; the effective constraint (both together)
	  is unchanged.

	  Without it the transforms exist and nothing can turn them on, which
	  is the right shape for a node application that configures its own
	  channels in C.
